Finally, I have downloaded the Slashem exe and began to explore what it 
has in addition to nethack.  To see something new, I started a flame 
mage, a drow.  Drows are a kind of elves?

Switched to explore mode in the first turn, which was wise with 
hindsight, because flame mages seem to be difficult to keep alive 
(pathetic stats except for int which was 20 from the start).  Also, 
their pet flaming spheres are different from usual pets in some 
respects.  For example, they are a much lower level than shopkeepers or 
soldiers and attack them nonetheless.  Moreover, the attacked monster 
gets angry at you, which is also not the case with pets normally! So in 
no time I had an angry shopkeeper and an angry captain in a town in the 
regular dungeon (a feature that I liked - but I died there twice...).

At the bottom of mines, I found a blood-red potion left by a vampire. 
Quaffed it and became a vampire myself.  It might be a potion of 
polymorph, but I suspect, it rather is blood, so I may even be a vampire 
permanently now.  Then I went to find the luckstone.  There was a gray 
stone in a small room.  Kicked it to make sure it was not a load stone. 
  It went down into a pit.  Here is what I consider a possible bug.  I 
could not take it out of the pit, because a vampire is flying...  Now, a 
true vampire could surely pick up things from the floor (mine can) and 
so should be able to descend into the pit to pick up the stone.  Also, I 
can #sit on the gray stone - which turns out not to be very comfortable 
- but if I want to grab it afterwards, I can't, because I cannot reach 
the bottom.  Is there a way to get to things in a pit for vampires?  (I 
don't have a wand of teleportation, which I would try else.)
